# Command buildah

## What does this command do:

A tool that facilitates building OCI images.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: sudo dnf -y install buildah

## Command path

For Fedora run: /usr/bin/buildah

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/containers/buildah/blob/main/install.md

## Command options

# Build an image from a Containerfile/Dockerfile
buildah build -t <image-name> .
buildah build -f <Containerfile> -t <image-name> .

# Create a working container from a base image
buildah from <image>

# List working containers
buildah containers

# List images in local storage
buildah images

# Copy content into a working container
buildah copy <container> <src> <dst>

# Add content to a working container
buildah add <container> <src> <dst>

# Run a command inside a working container
buildah run <container> -- <command>

# Update image configuration (labels, env, entrypoint, etc.)
buildah config --label <key>=<value> <container>
buildah config --env <key>=<value> <container>
buildah config --entrypoint '["cmd"]' <container>

# Commit a working container to an image
buildah commit <container> <image-name>

# Push an image to a registry
buildah push <image-name> docker://<registry>/<image>:<tag>

# Pull an image
buildah pull <image>

# Tag an image
buildah tag <image> <new-name>:<tag>

# Remove a working container
buildah rm <container>

# Remove an image
buildah rmi <image>

# Login/logout to a container registry
buildah login <registry>
buildah logout <registry>

# Mount a working container's root filesystem
buildah mount <container>
buildah umount <container>

# Inspect a container or image
buildah inspect <container-or-image>

# Manage manifest lists (multi-arch images)
buildah manifest create <list-name>
buildah manifest add <list-name> <image>
buildah manifest push <list-name> docker://<registry>/<image>:<tag>

# Prune build and mount cache
buildah prune

# Run command in a modified user namespace (rootless builds)
buildah unshare <command>

# Display version information
buildah version
